{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan review BLOCK, correctly. AC1 offered three acceptable liveness forms and one of them — 'an asserted exit code' — cannot distinguish an executed-and-denied child from one that never launched, since a sandbox that fails to start also exits non-zero. That is precisely the ambiguity this ticket exists to remove, so offering it as sufficient would have let the fix reintroduce the bug.\n\nAC1 now requires liveness evidence produced BY THE CHILD after it started (a sentinel written to an allowed path, or a marker on stdout), asserted before the denial is read, and explicitly disqualifies the wrapper's exit status."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787879551651426001,"uuid":"169f9d03-9b96-47f8-b6d0-33ead832df33"}